From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] Plutonium: Ash in shell mode

Ash's own UI gets out of the way of the shell page: accelerators and gestures go to the shell, and there are no toasts, nudges or clipboard history.

It holds these changes:
- no clipboard history nudges in shell mode
- a touchpad swipe's begin and end keep their finger count
- no Ash toasts, nudges or clipboard history, no Chrome toasts or clipboard bubble over the shell

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- pointer capture (lock, confine) for embedded apps, Super+Escape
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- the hardware keys go to the helper's desktop services; the browser's media session in the Plutonium domain
- touchpad swipes with three fingers or more go to the shell page
---
